    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12366" root="درب" body-key="d">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ادرب القَوْمُ</span></b>  <i>The people,</i> or <i>party, entered a
land of the enemy pertaining to the territory of
the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُوم</span> [or <i>people of the Greek Empire</i>]. (S.)
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدْرَبْنَا</span> occurs in a trad. as meaning <i>We entered
the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرْب</span> [q. v.]. (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ادرب</span> <i>He beat a drum;</i>
(IAar, T, TA;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرْدَبَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَبْدَبَ</span>. (TA.)

